<%#
  The three ticketing fee facts, reused on /, /for-producers and /pricing.
  The per-ticket figure comes from TicketPricing so the marketing copy can't
  drift from what checkout actually charges.
%>
<% ticket_fee = TicketPricing::PLATFORM_FEE_CENTS %>
<div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
  <div class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-pink-500 bg-white p-6">
    <div class="text-4xl font-bold text-pink-500 coustard-regular"><%= ticket_fee %>¢</div>
    <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 mt-1">per paid ticket. That's it.</div>
    <div class="text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1 leading-relaxed">
      No monthly ticketing fee, no setup fee, no percentage of the sale. A $20 ticket costs you <%= ticket_fee %>¢ to sell.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
    <div class="text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 coustard-regular">$0</div>
    <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 mt-1">for free tickets, comps &amp; cash at the door</div>
    <div class="text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1 leading-relaxed">
      Free shows, comped guests, and cash sales at the door carry no fee at all. You only pay when a ticket is paid for.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
    <div class="text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 coustard-regular">At cost</div>
    <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 mt-1">standard card processing, nothing added</div>
    <div class="text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1 leading-relaxed">
      Whatever the card processor charges passes straight through — no markup, and once per order rather than per ticket. You choose whether the buyer pays it or you absorb it.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
